Established in 2004, OLIVER is the world's first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&nbsp;
As a part of The Brandtech Group, we're at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our AI solutions enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&nbsp;Role:&nbsp; Senior Integrated Designer - 12 month FTC
Location:&nbsp; London, United Kingdom &nbsp;
About the role:&nbsp;
As Senior Integrated Designer,&nbsp;you'll&nbsp;lead creative thinking and execution across the studio's full channel mix, from&nbsp;initial&nbsp;concept through to final delivery across digital, social, motion, print, and events.&nbsp;You'll&nbsp;bring both ideas and craft to every brief, ensuring work is visually strong, strategically considered, and consistent across touchpoints and markets.&nbsp;
Operating within a regulated financial services environment,&nbsp;you'll&nbsp;bring discipline to compliance-sensitive materials, set quality benchmarks for the team, embed AI-assisted design workflows, and help build a studio the wider organisation is proud of.&nbsp;
What you will be doing:&nbsp;
&nbsp;Integrated Design &amp; Creative Production&nbsp;

Concept and create on-brand integrated work across the full channel mix, brand campaigns, digital and social content, motion, print, events,&nbsp;marketing collateral,&nbsp;thought leadership, and long-form communications, from brief through to final delivery&nbsp;
Bring integrated thinking to every brief, considering how ideas translate across channels, formats, and markets before execution begins&nbsp;
Produce motion and animation work for digital and social, applying strong storytelling and timing principles alongside visual craft&nbsp;
Adapt integrated design solutions for seven markets and multiple product lines,&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;visual and conceptual consistency within brand guardrails; prepare all files to correct digital, motion, and print specifications&nbsp;
Manage multiple live projects simultaneously,&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;brand integrity, quality standards, and deadlines across all output&nbsp;

&nbsp;Brand Guardianship &amp; Consistency&nbsp;

Champion consistency of visual identity, tone, and quality across every touchpoint and market, proactively&nbsp;identifying&nbsp;opportunities to strengthen brand expression&nbsp;
Apply compliance requirements,&nbsp;disclaimers, substantiation standards, and sign-off checkpoints,&nbsp;as standard practice, with approvals documented correctly&nbsp;
Contribute to brand guidelines, scalable templates, and asset systems that enable speed and consistency across the studio&nbsp;

&nbsp;Team Leadership &amp; Collaboration&nbsp;

Lead, direct, and mentor the design team, providing clear creative briefs, constructive feedback, and development support that raises capability and output quality across the integrated mix&nbsp;
Work closely with the embedded team and client stakeholders to develop integrated creative ideas, translating feedback into clear direction for the team&nbsp;

&nbsp;Gen AI &amp; Agentic Thinking&nbsp;

Apply advanced AI tools to enhance integrated creative output and workflows,&nbsp;building effective prompts, critically evaluating results, and&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;rigorous human oversight of quality and compliance&nbsp;
Design and embed AI-assisted workflows for the team, setting quality benchmarks and guiding responsible AI use across sizing, adaptation, motion, transcreation, and production efficiency&nbsp;
Break down complex, multi-format creative challenges into clear steps, leading the team to the best outcome efficiently and adapting confidently when priorities shift&nbsp;

What you need to be great in this role:&nbsp;

A strong portfolio&nbsp;demonstrating&nbsp;integrated creative thinking and execution across digital, social, motion, print, and campaign formats, with evidence of both conceptual originality and hands-on craft&nbsp;
Advanced&nbsp;proficiency&nbsp;across Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop, After Effects) and Figma; expert understanding of graphic design, typography, motion, and digital production standards&nbsp;
Proven ability to concept ideas that work across channels, not just adapt static design to new formats&nbsp;
Experience producing motion and animation work for digital and social, with strong storytelling instincts alongside technical execution&nbsp;
Experience producing integrated work for international or multi-market campaigns, adapting design systems across countries and channels within brand guardrails&nbsp;
Deep understanding of brand identity systems, able to apply, protect, and evolve visual standards across a complex, multi-touchpoint portfolio&nbsp;
Familiarity with regulated industries (financial services, insurance, or similar), or&nbsp;demonstrated&nbsp;ability to work within compliance, legal, and governance frameworks&nbsp;
Experience contributing to brand guidelines, scalable templates, and asset systems that enable consistency and speed across a team&nbsp;
Experience leading and mentoring designers, providing clear creative direction, developmental feedback, and coaching that builds integrated craft capability&nbsp;
Confident presenting and defending integrated creative concepts to senior stakeholders, translating feedback into clear direction for the team&nbsp;
Advanced use of AI tools relevant to integrated design, building effective workflows, evaluating outputs critically, and training others in responsible AI use&nbsp;
Agentic mindset: able to lead a team through complex, multi-format creative challenges, adapting confidently when priorities shift and&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;quality under pressure
Formal degrees are welcome but not required. Equivalent experience counts. Experience can be gained through work, study, volunteering, or self-directed learning.

