an&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt;showcases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt; the innovation behind over 550 patents in AI-driven generative design, materials, and additive manufacturing. With our three core pillars of dominating performance, iconic design, and revolutionary technology, Czinger is at the intersection of deep technology, consumer products, and high-performance branding. We invite you to join our world-class talent in shaping the future of the automotive industry. Here, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt;you&#39;ll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TrackChangeTextInsertion TrackedChange SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot;&gt; be part of a groundbreaking journey that pushes the limits of performance, design, technology, and sustainability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP TrackedChange CommentStart CommentHighlightPipeRestV2 PointComment CommentHighlightRest SCXW144108776 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Quality Engineer is responsible for driving quality performance across the assigned products and supplier base throughout the full product lifecycle, from supplier development and production readiness through launch, current production and issue resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary responsibility for this role is the Chassis vehicle system, with additional execution support for selected Powertrain suppliers and activities within the UK, including the Powertrain Controls interface. The role requires a high level of ownership, practical judgement and technical understanding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective cross functional collaboration to identify quality risks early, develop effective solutions and ensure robust implementation. Working closely with Engineering, Manufacturing, Supply Chain and suppliers, the Senior Quality Engineer will take ownership of quality concerns, drive supplier performance and support the continuous improvement of Quality Engineering processes, standards and practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Supplier Development &amp;amp; Production Readiness&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support supplier selection by assessing manufacturing capability, process maturity and identify key quality risks and required actions before supplier nomination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply the Supplier Qualification Framework and lead or coordinate the appropriate APQP, PPAP, audit and production-readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review key manufacturing controls, including FMEAs, Control Plans, inspection strategy, process capability and validation evidence, challenging gaps and driving actions where controls are not adequate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier-development actions and ensure significant supplier or manufacturing changes receive appropriate validation and requalification before implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Supplier Execution &amp;amp; Current Quality&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Quality Engineering follow-up for assigned suppliers and components &amp;nbsp;after launch, monitoring performance and emerging risks, proactively driving improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead containment, root-cause analysis and corrective action for significant supplier-related concerns, verifying sustainable prevention of recurrence, including clear ownership, timing and evidence of effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine when supplier visits, additional controls, escalation or supplier-development activities are required, using risk and data to determine the appropriate level of response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and coordinate incoming inspection requirements for assigned parts when defined by the Supplier Qualification Framework or required as part of issue containment, including stock checks, increased inspection and verification of subsequent purchase orders until confidence in product quality is restored.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide local UK execution support for selected Powertrain suppliers while maintaining alignment with the Powertrain system owner and relevant Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Product Quality &amp;amp; Ticket Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and coordinate the Product-quality ticket landscape for the assigned vehicle system, including Issues, Enhancements, FAR’s (Field Action Requests) and other applicable concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure concerns are clearly defined, prioritised and progressed with appropriate containment, technical ownership and corrective action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate resolution across Engineering, Manufacturing, Supply Chain and suppliers, clearly escalating significant or ageing risks when progress is insufficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain alignment between supplier-level actions and Product-level resolution, including support to Powertrain activities when assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Quality Documentation &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development, implementation and continuous improvement of Quality Engineering standards and documentation, using lessons learned from practical supplier and product quality experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure applicable requirements are understood and consistently deployed internally and within the supplier base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture lessons learned from supplier and Product-quality concerns into standards covering areas such as qualification, APQP/PPAP, inspection, critical characteristics, supplier changes and structured problem solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote effective and proportionate quality controls without unnecessary complexity or bureaucracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and a track record of taking complex issues through to effective closure, with the ability to work independently and make sound decisions in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience in Quality Engineering, Supplier Quality, Manufacturing Engineering or a related technical environment, ideally within a high-complexity manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with suppliers and manufacturing processes, with sound structured problem-solving capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of APQP, PPAP, FMEA, Control Plans and production-process qualification, with the ability to apply these tools practically and proportionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand engineering drawings, specifications and technical requirements, and translate them into practical quality controls. Previous GD&amp;amp;T experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working cross-functionally and constructively challenging suppliers or internal stakeholders when required, whilst maintaining effective working relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritise in a fast-moving environment, combining a practical, data-driven approach with sound judgement, and focus effort on the highest quality risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, curiosity and willingness to develop a detailed understanding of the product and manufacturing process, with the ability to communicate technical quality risks clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within automotive, motorsport, aerospace or other high-complexity manufacturing environments is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chassis or Powertrain experience is advantageous but not essential where strong transferable technical capability can be demonstrated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with low-volume, high value, high performance and technically complex products is particularly relevant to the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onsite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£71,971&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£98,963 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package: &lt;/strong&gt;Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment: &lt;/strong&gt;Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;CZV, Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. CZV, Inc. provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;EEO Poster&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We see the world differently at Capstone Investment Advisors. You will, too.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capstone Investment Advisors, LLC (“Capstone”) is a global asset manager, dedicated to exploring alpha opportunities in derivatives and complementary strategies that persist across market cycles. With approximately $12.5 billion of AUM (as of May 1, 2026) and 306 employees, Capstone is headquartered in New York with offices in London, Amsterdam, Stamford, Los Angeles, Boston, Tokyo, Milan, Texas, and Maryland. Since 2004, through strategic insight, market-leading expertise, and advanced technology, we have sought to anticipate and harness the complexities of world markets, creating unique opportunities for our clients, team, and industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our sophisticated, global client base, we recognize that our success is deeply connected to real people. For that reason, we take a human approach to everything we do, focusing largely on collaborative performance. Our workflow and process are built around the belief that by sharing ideas, we achieve greater outcomes. This gives you greater access to resources, direct exposure to senior leadership, and new opportunities to experiment and innovate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capstone is looking to appoint a Senior Risk Engineer at Senior Vice President level within Risk Technology. This is a hands-on role combining software engineering, risk and financial markets, with direct exposure to the investment process. You will design and build investment-facing risk and decision-support capabilities, remaining close to the code, data and users from initial problem through to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to build the technology behind Capstone’s Risk Intelligence strategy - turning complex risk and portfolio data into timely, actionable intelligence. You will develop tools that help Portfolio Managers and Risk Managers understand what changed, what drove it and what action to consider across stress scenarios, risk factors, margin, liquidity and portfolio analytics. The work will directly support sizing, trade expression, hedging, portfolio construction and capital allocation - helping drive better decisions, more efficient capital and more repeatable alpha.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Risk Managers, Portfolio Managers, Quant Research and the wider Technology, Data and AI teams. The role requires deep technical contribution, end-to-end ownership and the ability to shape outcomes through strong judgement, delivery and collaboration. It offers broad exposure across strategies and asset classes, together with the opportunity to help shape the next generation of Capstone’s Risk Technology platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a high-performing team that values ownership, collaboration and solving difficult problems. We encourage curiosity and new ideas, alongside the discipline and reliability needed to deliver and support critical production systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, build and own production-grade components of Capstone’s Risk Technology platform, remaining close to the code, data and users and designing for performance, scalability, reliability and usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve scalable cross-asset risk capabilities spanning Greeks and sensitivities, stress scenarios, VaR, P&amp;amp;L vectors and attribution, limits, factor analytics, margin, and exposure aggregation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with Portfolio Managers, Risk Managers and Quant Research to solve complex derivatives, risk and portfolio challenges, taking ideas from problem definition through to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build APIs, data pipelines and interactive decision tools that help users understand what changed, what drove it and what action to consider at trade, POD, strategy and fund level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate pricing and risk methodologies into scalable, explainable services, with clear treatment of model assumptions, calibration, validation and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance Capstone’s Risk Intelligence strategy by building tools that turn research, risk analytics and AI into practical investment insight - helping Portfolio Managers and Risk Managers analyse scenarios, understand book and factor exposures, diagnose P&amp;amp;L and access validated analytics through natural language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer and operate resilient risk services, integrating positions, market and reference data, and internal or third-party analytics, with strong testing, data lineage and end-to-end ownership of production issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and deliver high-value components of the Risk Technology roadmap in partnership with Technology, Data and AI teams, using common platforms, standards and engineering practices and contributing to design reviews, code reviews and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our future colleague has these skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant experience in software engineering, quantitative development or risk technology within a hedge fund, asset manager, investment bank or comparable capital-markets environment, with meaningful exposure to front-office or market-risk systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of personally designing, building and supporting production-grade risk, pricing or trading systems, and owning complex projects from definition through delivery and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Python / Java and SQL skills, together with strong proficiency in at least one comparable language; practical experience with APIs, distributed or event-driven architectures, databases, data pipelines and large-scale processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of derivatives and cross-asset risk analytics, including option pricing, Greeks, scenario analysis and VaR. Knowledge of factor risk and margin analytics is desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architecture and engineering judgement, with a focus on maintainability, testability, performance, controls and operational resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to critically assess model outputs, challenge assumptions and trace discrepancies across data, calibration, methodology and implementation, while explaining conclusions clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating internally developed and third-party pricing and risk libraries across asset classes, with strong attention to data lineage, reconciliation, consistency and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communication and evidence of technical leadership through judgement, ownership, and delivery, with the ability to collaborate effectively with Portfolio Managers, Risk Managers, Quant Research and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_x_x_x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Bonus skills:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience applying machine learning, large language models agentic tools or AI-assisted development in a controlled production environment, including evaluation, access controls, monitoring and human oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating modern engineering and data platforms, including cloud infrastructure, containers, CI/CD, streaming, data lineage and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep product and risk knowledge in at least one asset class, combined with a broad working understanding across multiple asset classes, including equities, fixed income, credit, commodities and FX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Compensation Information:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is our most important asset and investment. We value and respect our colleagues and their well-being inside and outside the workplace and our culture reflects this.&amp;nbsp; We offer a robust and competitive benefits program to ensure the well-being of our colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some benefits included in this role are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust Wellness Resources: Physical, Mental and Financial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time-Off, Retirement and Commuter Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gym Reimbursement and other Discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay offered will be determined on factors such as experience, skills, training, location, certifications, education, and any applicable minimum wage requirements. Decisions will be determined on a case-by-case basis. In addition to the base salary, this position may be eligible for performance-based incentives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base compensation, this role is eligible for an annual incentive plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn even more about being part of the team, visit us online: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.capstoneco.com/careers/&quot;&gt;Careers - Capstone (capstoneco.com)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don’t forget to follow us on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/capstone-investment-advisors/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capstone’s Commitment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Capstone, we value a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace where all employees feel appreciated and respected. Our commitment to a nondiscriminatory approach extends equal opportunities for employment and advancement across our programs, departments, and locations. We actively seek and appreciate a variety of life experiences and heritages and advocate for the amplification of all voices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Capstone, we&#39;re all about creating a workplace where you can thrive and make a real impact. We value innovation, teamwork, trust, and discipline, and we know you do too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt; We love fresh ideas and encourage you to try new things. Here, you’ll have the freedom to innovate and help shape our strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; We’re big on teamwork. You&#39;ll join a supportive community where everyone’s input matters, and we learn from each other every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust:&lt;/strong&gt; We believe in building strong, honest relationships. You&#39;ll be part of an environment where your contributions are respected and integrity is key.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discipline:&lt;/strong&gt; In our fast-paced world, staying focused is crucial. We commit to high standards and a disciplined approach, helping you grow both personally and professionally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team that values your creativity and dedication. Together, let&#39;s push boundaries and achieve great things.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Capstone is committed to creating an inclusive environment where we welcome people of different backgrounds. Capstone considers applications for employment without regard to all applicable protected characteristics, including race, color, religion, ethnicity, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, parental status, veteran status, or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Buildkite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Buildkite&#39;s CI platform is trusted by the world&#39;s leading engineering teams, helping ship software used by more than 1 billion people every day. Companies including Canva, Meta, Mistral AI, and NVIDIA rely on Buildkite to run builds, tests, and deployments on their infrastructure, ours, or both - giving them the speed, reliability, and flexibility to ship with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not your average Support Engineer role. You&#39;ll support Buildkite&#39;s enterprise customers by independently troubleshooting and resolving highly complex CI/CD, software, and infrastructure problems, collaborating directly with Software Engineering teams at places like Canva, Uber, and Airbnb to help unblock critical workflows. You&#39;ll play a vital role in shaping the support team&#39;s evolution into a function that balances reactive and proactive work, spending half your time designing and implementing scalable tools, processes, and open source contributions that create a world-class customer experience. This role is a perfect opportunity for a Software, DevOps, or Infrastructure expert who is customer obsessed and thrives on solving tough technical problems for some of the world&#39;s most innovative engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is remote and requires someone to be located in the UK, Ireland or Poland. You&#39;ll work five days a week, 9:00 AM–5:00 PM local time, &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;including both Saturday and Sunday&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;. Your other three days are flexible — we&#39;ll agree on a set schedule together when you join.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently resolve highly technical CI/CD, software, and infrastructure issues for enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support through Slack, Zoom, Email, Plain, and Community Forum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer-facing retrospectives and planning sessions to improve their Buildkite experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to prevent future support issues and drive the design and implementation of proactive solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and maintain open source tools such as Bash plugins and Golang-based utilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish documentation updates and proactive communications that improve the customer journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a voice for customers, ensuring their feedback shapes internal product and process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve support workflows, simplifying how the team operates and delivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share learnings from customer work to strengthen alignment with Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor peers and foster an inclusive, supportive environment within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Is You If You Have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Centric Mindset&lt;/strong&gt; – Deep commitment to delivering world-class support with empathy and patience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Expertise&lt;/strong&gt; – Strong coding or scripting ability with experience in Bash, Ruby on Rails, or Golang&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps and Cloud Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt; – Solid experience with CI/CD tools and platforms including Linux, AWS, GCP, Azure, Terraform, and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving Skills&lt;/strong&gt; – Confident in independently tackling complex technical issues and guiding customers to solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous and Proactive&lt;/strong&gt; – Able to work independently, identify opportunities early, and take initiative to drive meaningful improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Skilled at articulating technical detail clearly to customers and internal teams across distributed environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;20 days paid annual leave plus 10 days sick &amp;amp; carer&#39;s leave&lt;/strong&gt; — actively encouraged, we want you to be at your best and time off is a part of that.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ongoing remote-work allowance to help you do your best work&lt;/strong&gt; — we want you to have everything you need, from great wifi to wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement and health coverage &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(based on your region)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;— build towards your future, your way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave for primary carers (6 weeks for secondary)&lt;/strong&gt; — becoming a parent is life changing and we’re committed to supporting you and your family through it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confidential EAP &amp;amp; mental health support&lt;/strong&gt; — sometimes life gets hard. You should be able to access the resources and support you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support for learning and growth&lt;/strong&gt; — with time and budget for conferences, courses, and coaching so you have the opportunity to grow, improve your craft, and build mastery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility to work from anywhere in the world for up to 6 weeks a year&lt;/strong&gt; — great work doesn’t have to happen from one desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exact benefits may vary slightly by country. We&#39;ll walk through the specifics for your location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Buildkite, we value diversity and celebrate all types of skills, backgrounds, and experiences. We’re dedicated to fostering an inclusive environment and providing reasonable accommodations throughout our recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need any accommodations or support during the application or interview process, please reach out to us at -----Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Marketing Manager – Connected Cloud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary: Competitive depending on experience, plus bonus and benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Hybrid, with an expectation of two days a week in the office (London or Longbridge)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kerv Connect Cloud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kerv is a purpose‑led UK cloud and digital services organisation supporting mid‑market and enterprise customers to design, deliver, and operate technology platforms that enable meaningful business change. Through a set of specialist practices, Kerv brings deep expertise across cloud, digital transformation, networking, security, and compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kerv Connected Cloud (KCC) brings together end‑user services, networking, security, and cloud managed services to deliver secure, resilient, and scalable digital foundations. We design, implement, and operate connected cloud environments that underpin modern workplaces and business‑critical services, combining strong technical foundations with operational discipline to help customers transform with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a commercially focused marketing leader to drive growth across our Connected Cloud practice. Reporting to the CMO and sitting within the marketing leadership team, you&#39;ll own the Connected Cloud marketing strategy, budget, campaigns, and pipeline performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your focus will be generating qualified pipeline, delivering measurable results, and building strong relationships with sales, solutions, and strategic partners including Microsoft, TD Synnex and Juniper.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with the Connected Cloud MD, Sales Director and Chief Solutions Officer, you&#39;ll ensure marketing supports business growth across key sectors including retail, professional services, legal and public sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Pipeline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Connected Cloud marketing plan, budget and pipeline targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver lead generation, opportunity creation and pipeline growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a rolling campaign plan, continually measuring and optimising performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make investment decisions based on commercial outcomes and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaigns &amp;amp; Proposition Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take networking, cloud, managed services and AI-enabled workplace propositions to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver both demand generation and account-based marketing campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief and collaborate with central marketing teams across content, design, digital, PR and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and insight to refine messaging and improve results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alliances &amp;amp; Partner Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead marketing relationships with Microsoft, TD Synnex, Juniper and other partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure and manage MDF and co-funded marketing activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build campaigns that strengthen the Kerv brand while maximising partner investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Alignment &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with sales to define lead management, attribution and reporting standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Dynamics 365 and marketing data to demonstrate pipeline contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular reporting on campaign performance, pipeline and partner funding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success building B2B pipeline within technology services, managed services or the Microsoft partner ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning marketing targets, budgets and commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong alliance and partner marketing experience, including MDF management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of cloud, networking, managed services and modern workplace technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering demand generation and ABM programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong CRM, reporting and data analysis skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel and attend the London office at least one day per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to public sector organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of retail, legal or professional services sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Microsoft partner programmes, Dynamics 365 and Power BI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous team leadership experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact leadership role with clear accountability for Connected Cloud marketing performance. You&#39;ll have ownership of budget, strategy and results, access to specialist marketing resources, and the opportunity to shape a growing practice while directly influencing business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kerv values…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Think Customer First&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Team is everything&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Spread good vibes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build future&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Do the right thing&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Kerv, we’re building something special and we’re building it to last. We want everybody to feel valued, included and love working together. With an uncompromising pursuit of amazing employee experience, we always strive to do the right thing. We believe and will relentlessly promote and support the power of diversity, equality&amp;nbsp;and belonging, through&amp;nbsp;collaboration and creating exceptional solutions together.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will live the Kerv values…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think Customer First&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team is everything&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spread good vibes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the right thing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Kerv, we’re building something special and we’re building it to last. We want everybody to feel valued, included and love working together. With an uncompromising pursuit of amazing employee experience, we always strive to do the right thing. We believe and will relentlessly promote and support the power of diversity, equality and belonging, through collaboration and creating exceptional solutions together.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Consulting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;London&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract type:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;6-Month FTC&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Time/Part time:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Full time&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting into:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Consulting Partner&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ogilvy:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy UK has been creating iconic ideas that deliver impact at scale for clients ever since David Ogilvy founded the company in 1948. Ogilvy UK specialises in bringing together brand advertising, customer experience marketing, PR, influence and consulting, all fuelled by Behavioural Science. Our world-class award-winning creative campaigns deliver solutions for clients including Molson Coors (owner of Madrí beer), Valeo Foods UK (owner of Kettle Chips and Rowse Honey), Argos, Mondelēz International, Unilever, TK Maxx and Pernod Ricard.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2023, Ogilvy UK celebrated their 75th anniversary and was the most awarded agency in Europe. Ogilvy is home to the largest influencer marketing practice globally and hosts the world’s biggest festival of behavioural science and creativity, Nudgestock – now in its 12th year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy Consulting is a brand-led growth consultancy, nestled at the heart of the world-leading Ogilvy creative group. We tackle complex and rewarding challenges for some of the world’s most loved businesses and brands, as well as fast-growing scale-ups, and we’re proud to have been named as one of the FT’s UK leading management consultancies for the seventh consecutive year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s an exciting time to be joining Ogilvy Consulting. As we grow, we’re looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Consultant to join our Marketing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; practice.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Senior Consultants&lt;/strong&gt; bring&amp;nbsp;a&amp;nbsp;unique blend of creative thinking, strategic depth and analytical&amp;nbsp;rigour. They are broad thinkers and practical problem-solvers, emerging in a specialist area of marketing transformation while remaining grounded in strong core consulting skills. They help clients understand how marketing organisations, capabilities, ways of working and operating models need to evolve to unlock growth, improve effectiveness and respond to a digitally led, AI-enabled world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires experience in supporting and delivering marketing transformation work. We work across areas such as organisational design, target operating model definition, change management, capability building, process mapping, employee experience and AI advisory. Senior Consultants play a critical role in translating this thinking into practical workstreams, high-quality deliverables and clear recommendations that clients can act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key&amp;nbsp;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning discrete workstreams within wider marketing transformation projects, working independently with appropriate oversight and directing junior team members where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the design and delivery of transformation work across operating model design, organisational design, change management, capability building, process mapping, employee experience and AI-enabled marketing transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with colleagues across the Consulting team and the wider Ogilvy and WPP network to solve high-profile challenges for our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying relevant consulting methodologies to structure analysis, frame hypotheses, build recommendations and create high-quality client deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building trusted working relationships with mid-level client teams, confidently facilitating meetings, leading interviews, capturing key insights and helping maintain momentum across project activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in strategic new business pitches and initiatives, including preparing sections of proposals and identifying add-on opportunities within existing client relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping abreast of developments in marketing transformation, modern operating models, organizational change, AI and marketing effectiveness, actively contributing to the team’s knowledge base and thought leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as a role model for your grade, supporting Analysts and Consultants, helping onboard new colleagues and contributing to a positive, inclusive and high-performing project environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Attributes and Attitude:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience in consulting, client-side strategy, marketing transformation, organizational change or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emerging specialist expertise in one or more areas of marketing transformation such as operating model design, organizational design, change management, capability building, employee experience, process design or AI-enabled marketing transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, with the ability to synthesise quantitative and qualitative inputs, identify key trends and develop clear, actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of, and interest in, behavioural science and the principles of behaviour change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to prepare and lead client interviews, workshops and meetings, using active listening to draw out insight, align stakeholders and move teams toward practical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort challenging conventional views and presenting ideas persuasively to gain buy-in from clients and colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of modern marketing organisations and how brands, capabilities, technology, data, process and culture come together to drive growth and effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI and its impact on marketing transformation, with the ability to identify opportunities to use AI tools and methodologies to improve insight, efficiency and project workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the energy, pragmatism and flexibility to thrive in a fast-moving consulting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ogilvy Consulting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy Consulting is different from other consultancies: we bridge strategy and execution, rigour and creativity. We are nestled at the heart of Ogilvy and the broader WPP network, which means we can bring together consulting, creative, data, technology, media and experience expertise to help clients move from strategy to implementation. We’re also organised differently, with a flat hierarchy designed to provide opportunities for meaningful contributions by team members at all levels. Alongside Marketing Transformation, we work across brand strategy, innovation, sustainability and behavioural science, and all team members have the opportunity to contribute to integrated projects across the Ogilvy Consulting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ogilvy Consulting has adopted a flexible working approach, with the ability to work from home and three days per week expected in the office with the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a deeply passionate group who enjoy the challenges and rewards of Consulting work in equal measures.&amp;nbsp;We are looking to scale the team with&amp;nbsp;talent&amp;nbsp;who are as ambitious as they are rigorous and innovative – people who see themselves advancing according to merit and&amp;nbsp;are&amp;nbsp;open to seizing the opportunities our&amp;nbsp;fast-moving growth environment offers.&amp;nbsp;If this sounds like you, please get in touch.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we help you Thrive:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days annual leave + 1 Volunteer Day&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bupa Healthcare&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Maternity, Adoption and Shared Parental Leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have a Flexible Working Model with core working hours: 10am – 4pm&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 1.5:1 Matching Pension Structure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing and Health: Up to £25.00 per month towards physical or online exercise class membership, Unmind membership, LifeWorks tool and annual eye tests and development budgets and Wellbeing incentives and activities throughout the year&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Season Ticket Loan and Cycle to Work Scheme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Our ambition is to attract the very best diverse talent to Ogilvy, and to be the employer of choice in the UK. We want everyone to feel welcome when they join us, and once they’re here, for them to want to stay with us, grow their career, and to feel they belong with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and we’re committed to creating an inclusive, welcoming environment for everyone who wants to work at Ogilvy. For us, diversity, equity and inclusion is integrated into everything that we do. We believe that for creativity to flourish, everything about how we work must have diversity at its core. Your race, colour, ethnic, religion, gender, gender identity, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, have no bearing on our hiring decisions, but we encourage everyone to feel free to express their true selves in an environment we are consistently striving to make as inclusive as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;We aim to facilitate an accessible and positive application experience for all candidates. If you require any adjustments from us to support you through the process or expect to require any adjustments to working conditions to be able to best perform in the role, please let us know. We are happy to consider all reasonable adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;If you live with a disability and you would like to take advantage of our offer of a guaranteed interview under the Disability Confident Scheme, please ensure you fill out our voluntary Equal Opportunities Questionnaire when applying.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

