&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;About Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_22f5dbaece6b7d09-108&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0&quot;&gt;Moniepoi&lt;span class=&quot;citation-45&quot;&gt;nt Group is a financial technology company digitizing Africa’s real economy by building a financial e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-44 citation-45 citation-end-45&quot;&gt;cosystem for businesses, providing them with all the payment, banking, credit and business management tools they &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-44 citation-end-44&quot;&gt;need to succeed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-43 citation-end-43&quot;&gt;. At Moniepoint, we are a customer-focused community, dedicated to crafting solutions that&lt;/span&gt; redefine our industry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-42 citation-end-42&quot;&gt;. We have several products that provide essential services for businesses such as credit, overdrafts, bank integration, payment gateway, etc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,6&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-41 citation-end-41&quot;&gt;. We leverage artificial intelligence and data to make our decisions, but a&lt;/span&gt;lso have the technology and data-driven best practices used to support our businesses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;About this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Content Designer, you take ownership of the quality and strategic direction of content across your squad or product area. You bring expert content design judgment, deep user insight, and a collaborative mindset to shape product experiences that are clear, inclusive, and emotionally engaging. You support junior content designers, influence cross-team content strategy, and play a vital role in driving alignment across product, design, and engineering. You display an exceptional grasp of design thinking and content design expertise and are comfortable delivering well-thought out ideas to senior stakeholders and driving content design strategy each day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are responsible for end-to-end content design strategy and execution on a project, from discovery through delivery, launch, and ongoing iteration. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering closely with product managers, product designers, and engineers to embed content strategy in product discovery and delivery, shaping scope, trade-offs, and sequencing. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define for exceptional, accessible, and inclusive content that builds trust, clarity, and meaningful user engagement. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable wireframing and prototyping and delivering your work in Figma, with clear rationale, adhering to a design systems and content design principles.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define content design strategy that aligns with business objectives and technical feasibility, ensuring content is not just clear but emotionally intelligent and on brand. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft high-quality content for complex product flows, interface text, microcopy, error messaging, help content, and documentation, setting the bar for tone, clarity, and consistency. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a strong role in qualitative and quantitative research methods (user interviews, usability tests, A/B experiments, content audits, analytics) using insight as a core design input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate deeply, proactively shaping product direction, surfacing trade-offs, and influencing delivery approaches. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the evolution of content design style guides, working closely with brand, marketing, and communications teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design thoughtful content that enhances usability, emotional impact, and user satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance speed and rigour with strong judgment on when to ship versus polish, especially on complex or fast-moving environments. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support junior content designers on the team and supports in terms of stakeholder management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead alignment and collaboration across teams and stakeholders, clearly communicating content design rationale and facilitating strategic working sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high standard for product teams, fostering a culture of sound content design practices, constructive feedback, and shared accountability. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to justify content design decisions to senior stakeholders with clear rationale and delivers work in a standardised format that you help to evolve. You are able to deliver multiple variations, informed by insights and can confidently explain the pros and cons of particular solutions.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to succeed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working as a content designer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are incredibly comfortable with the design aspect of content design – understanding this role is deeper than &#39;just words&#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills are a must for this role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must be able to work in a fast-changing environment where processes are still being defined.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional knowledge of content design principles and end-to-end product thinking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with A/B testing, UX metrics, and data interpretation and the ability to drive your own research initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional product intuition - understanding user needs, business constraints, and technical feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good knowledge of Figma - how to collaborate, create prototypes, and work to produce agile solutions quickly, with little to no help.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI a plus. Great if you’ve built workflows/tools using AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent knowledge of working in cross-functional teams. Able to advocate for content design across various company areas and embed content design early in product planning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contributes to a content design system, creating reusable patterns and components &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech or SaaS environments is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills - able to explain the “why” behind your decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management is a must for this role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application &amp;amp; portfolio review&lt;/strong&gt; - we’re looking for exceptional content design case studies, showing examples of end-to-end product thinking, driven by research and illustrating impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiter conversation&lt;/strong&gt; - light intro on your background, team experience, and motivations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership interview&lt;/strong&gt; - deep dive into your skills and expertise with the lead content designer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content design task and portfolio presentation &lt;/strong&gt;- a short task to assess how you approach content design and you’ll present a case study from your portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions. Through our subsidiaries, Moniepoint Inc. processes over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Senior Business Analyst plays a key role in shaping the growth and success of Moniepoint’s payment products. You&#39;ll design, test, and implement strategies that improve user acquisition, boost retention, and elevate product engagement.&amp;nbsp;This role blends deep quantitative analysis with collaborative, strategic thinking. You&#39;ll partner with teams across the business to ensure our payment solutions meet real market demands and grow efficiently as we scale. Ultimately, you&#39;ll make sure our products not only attract users but also scale sustainably to create financial happiness for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Curious about what makes Moniepoint an incredible place to work?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://moniepoint.com/blog&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Check out posts on how we cultivate a culture of innovation, teamwork, and growth.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product managers, business development, and data engineering teams to help our growth team uncover problems and make product metrics highly visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex product and business questions into simple, actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and scale self-service dashboards and custom visualisation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end analytics for our growth products—from gathering data requirements and estimating opportunity sizes to designing experiments and conducting post-launch impact reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate trusted relationships across teams, acting as a collaborative link between technology, business, and product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply advanced mathematical and statistical modelling techniques (including A/B tests, multivariate testing, clustering, and supervised learning) to solve practical business problems that drive high-impact results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 to 4 years of professional experience (excluding academic projects and internships) in a quantitative analysis role within high-scale tech companies, tier-1 consulting firms, or investment banks with strong programming demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent SQL skills (which we will test during our interview process).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience designing, running, and analysing experiments on digital products (such as A/B and multivariate tests).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with popular visualisation tools like Tableau or Looker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying statistical modelling and advanced analytics to deliver practical, product-shaping insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in statistical programming (Python) and familiarity with tools like Pandas, SciPy, and Jupyter notebooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, professional spoken and written English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Science&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture - We put our people first and prioritise every team member&#39;s well-being. We’ve built a company where all opinions carry weight and where all voices are heard. We value and respect each other and always look out for one another. Above all, we are human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning - We have a learning and development-focused environment with an emphasis on knowledge sharing, training, and regular internal technical talks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation - You’ll receive an attractive salary, pension, health insurance, annual bonus, plus other benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect in the hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A preliminary phone call with one of our recruiters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A panel interview with a member of the hiring team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A behavioural and technical interview with a member of the Executive team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions. Through our subsidiaries, Moniepoint Inc. processes over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why United Kingdom&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK is home to our headquarters where more than 70 team members are based. Our London office is located at Sea Containers, just by London Bridge - this is also where a significant number of our most senior leaders sit, which makes it a natural base for a Head of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, now we are looking for our Head of Engineering, Supply Chain to join us in the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;POS Hardware and Device Platforms owns the software behind the physical side of Moniepoint&#39;s business: the systems that track, move, maintain and account for millions of POS terminals in the field. That covers inventory and warehouse management, logistics and distribution, repair and maintenance workflows, and the operational tooling the business runs on day to day. It is a backend and distributed systems challenge at real scale - making operational data about millions of physical devices visible, trustworthy and consistent across every market we operate in. It is not a hardware engineering role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Engineering, POS Supply Chain, oversees that software estate and is vital as Moniepoint expands internationally and scales device operations globally. The position involves leading the technical strategy for the domain and managing a large engineering organisation in a remote, distributed environment. As Head of Engineering, Supply Chain, your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the technical strategy and architecture for inventory and logistics tools and repair management software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading an engineering organisation of approximately 25 engineers, including managers, QA, SRE and Data Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving&amp;nbsp;platformisation of inventory and supply chain systems so operational data is visible, trustworthy and consistent across millions of terminals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridging the gap between operational practice and software systems by building operationally disciplined solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining architecture standards, engineering processes and quality metrics across squads to ensure reliability and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with business and operational stakeholders to translate operational requirements into engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring, mentoring and developing engineering managers and senior engineers to support team growth up to 30+ members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–15 years of overall software engineering experience, with at least 5 years leading engineering teams through growth phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on, production-level experience writing and shipping Java code as a practising engineer. This means years spent writing Java yourself, not years spent overseeing teams who write it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience managing managers - leading an engineering organisation through other engineering leaders, rather than running a single team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience in supply chain, inventory, warehouse or logistics software at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech or regulated-industry experience, with an understanding of the operational stakes of device management in a payments environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend engineering skills for data-intensive, distributed, operational systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven system design ability at large scale, managing hundreds of thousands of devices or more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and developing large engineering teams of 20 or more members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management, translating complex technical concepts for non-technical leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-minded approach to solving operational problems with engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultural Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As well, we assess every candidate across eight dimensions that define how great leaders operate at Moniepoint. We look for evidence of all eight throughout the process, not just in a single conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Obsession: Build deep empathy for users. Solve problems intuitively, and fix root causes, not just tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft: Master the fundamentals. Reason from first principles, make trade-offs explicit, and raise the bar on quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systemisation: Turn repeating decisions into scalable mechanisms. Reduce cognitive load and raise engineering quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Urgency: Move with disciplined speed. Act autonomously within scope, remove friction, and escalate risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership: Treat the platform as your own. Take initiative across boundaries and follow through without reminders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No Ego: Put the mission first. Share credit, welcome debate, and never protect status over team outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candour: Surface uncomfortable truths and risks early. Intelligent failure is welcome; concealment is not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity: Stay truthful and ethically consistent. Refuse toxic behavior. Performance without integrity is unacceptable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like In The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Scalable inventory and logistics systems delivered, supporting millions of devices across multiple countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A high-performing, motivated engineering team aligned with company growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Operational data visibility and trust established across multiple global markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Robust architecture standards enabling reliability and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Effective collaboration with business and operational teams to meet rapid expansion needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead engineering for one of Africa&#39;s largest POS networks and directly influence our global expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work in a fast-paced, innovative environment at the intersection of fintech and hardware operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be part of a mission-driven company impacting millions of businesses and individuals across Africa and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect in the hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A preliminary phone call with the recruiter.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;60 minute High level System Design round with one of our Engineering Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;60 minute Panel Interview with 2 of our Head of Engineering leaders, 30 minutes focused on a technical deep dive into your CV and into a project/system you built in the past. 30 minutes will be focused on testing for leadership attributes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;60 minute Stakeholder Management Round with one of our Product Heads/VPs, focused on your stakeholder management, collaboration skills with product/business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;60 minute Technical round and Culture fit interview with our Co-founder &amp;amp; Group CTO (the hiring manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions. Through our subsidiaries, Moniepoint Inc. processes over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why the UK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK is home to our headquarters where more than 70 team members are based, with team members joining us from companies like Tide, Klarna, Revolut, Capital One, Teya, Wise, Starling, Monzo, and many others! Our London office is located at Sea Containers, just by London Bridge - this is also where a significant number of our most senior leaders sit, which makes it a natural base for a Head of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, now we are looking for our Head of Engineering, Sales &amp;amp; Marketing Tools, to join us in UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sales and Marketing Tools owns MonieCRM, the operating system for Moniepoint&#39;s 50,000-strong sales network. This is not a CRM we bought — it is a workforce operations platform built entirely in-house for a multi-level field sales hierarchy, and it is how those teams run their day to day: the portfolio of businesses they manage, their own teams, their goals and performance, the physical and digital resources they need in the field, and an emerging AI-assisted support layer. Sixteen capabilities span onboarding and network management, pipeline and portfolio, performance and goals, compensation, and sales experience and support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A significant part of the domain moves money. The platform owns wallets, commission calculation and attribution, cashout and welfare funds for a network that drives the overwhelming majority of company revenue — which makes financial correctness, not just availability, a core engineering requirement of the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside that, the domain covers partner management, a rewards and retention platform serving tens of millions of users, and our marketing technology stack, including the engineering and customisation of Braze, the platform we use for customer engagement. The mandate is modernisation and reliability: re-architecting systems that have grown very quickly and making them dependable at a scale of more than 20 million users. This is a platform engineering and legacy modernisation challenge first and foremost, and prior CRM or SalesTech experience is genuinely not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 10–15 years of overall software engineering experience, with at least 5 years leading engineering teams through growth phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on, production-level experience writing and shipping Java code as a practising engineer. This means years spent writing Java yourself, not years spent overseeing teams who write it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience managing managers — leading an engineering organisation through other engineering leaders, rather than running a single team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have proven platform engineering experience at scale — building and running complex distributed systems, not feature delivery alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have navigated legacy migrations and re-architecture projects at 20M+ user scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong backend engineering skills in high-throughput, data-intensive distributed systems, and are proficient in Java and Spring Boot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have managed and developed large engineering teams of 20 or more members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building systems where financial correctness matters — commissions, payouts, wallets, ledgers or equivalent — is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fintech or payments background is strongly preferred. CRM or SalesTech domain experience is nice to have and explicitly not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to customer engagement or marketing automation platforms such as Braze is a plus, but not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultural Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As well, we assess every candidate across eight dimensions that define how great leaders operate at Moniepoint. We look for evidence of all eight throughout the process, not just in a single conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Obsession: Build deep empathy for users. Solve problems intuitively, and fix root causes, not just tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft: Master the fundamentals. Reason from first principles, make trade-offs explicit, and raise the bar on quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systemisation: Turn repeating decisions into scalable mechanisms. Reduce cognitive load and raise engineering quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Urgency: Move with disciplined speed. Act autonomously within scope, remove friction, and escalate risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership: Treat the platform as your own. Take initiative across boundaries and follow through without reminders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No Ego: Put the mission first. Share credit, welcome debate, and never protect status over team outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candour: Surface uncomfortable truths and risks early. Intelligent failure is welcome; concealment is not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity: Stay truthful and ethically consistent. Refuse toxic behavior. Performance without integrity is unacceptable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like In The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legacy systems modernised and re-architected, with measurable improvement in reliability and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commissions and earnings calculated, attributed and paid accurately and on time, at network scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sales and marketing platform that scales with a rapidly growing agent network across multiple markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial teams able to move faster because the tooling beneath them is dependable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high-performing engineering team with a strong bench of managers and senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the platform behind the commercial engine of one of Africa&#39;s largest digital banks — the system 50,000 people rely on to do their jobs and to get paid.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine platform modernisation mandate with the autonomy and backing to see it through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a mission-driven company impacting millions of businesses and individuals across Africa and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What To Expect In The Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute High level System Design round with one of our Engineering Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Panel Interview with 2 of our Head of Engineering leaders. 30 minutes focused on a technical deep dive into your CV and into a project or system you built in the past. 30 minutes focused on testing for leadership attributes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Stakeholder Management Round with one of our Product Heads/VPs, focused on your stakeholder management and collaboration skills with product and business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Technical round and Culture fit interview with our Co-founder &amp;amp; Group CTO (the hiring manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
